{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/700087-lunars-and-the-urban-jungle","id":700087,"title":"Lunars and the Urban Jungle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-13T13:54:53-07:00","id":700087,"title":"Lunars and the Urban Jungle","content":"<i>The following is from Oliver Falsefang, Changing Moon Lunar of Exalted Modern:</i><br /> So you heard those guys up top been talking about how Lunars do things like animals yeah? And I'm thinking your wondering: how does that fit into them interacting with civilization, you ask? Well never fear, Oliver Falsefang is here to teach you a little something about the urban jungle you see. You may think this is all civilized and soft and whatnot, but take it from someone who knows: the city can be dangerous. It may not have your predators leaping out with their big fangs and threatening eyes, but thats just it: the danger ain't obvious. You have to be wary, cause it won't let you know. There are a lot of predators in the city, and all of have smiling faces with perfect teeth and a contract to sign.<br /> <br /> Take for example,the used car salesman. Look at how he ensnares people with his pretty seeming words, gets them caught up in jargon they don't know about, offers them contracts full of hidden clauses and complicated words they won't bother to read. Look at how he takes advantage of their ignorance to sell them a bad car that will break down sooner or later to get their money. Just one of the more common predators of society, preying upon your money and desires to sell you garbage. Then of course there is the insurance salesman always parasitically draining away your money as long as nothing bad happens to you, something that works as long as your convinced that something bad COULD happen to you and you don't want to take the risk that you'll be caught up the creak without it, paying money when nothing bad happens to you on the hopes that you will get it all back when it eventually does, is there any better way to feed off your prey?<br /> <br /> That isn't physical enough for you? Well how about gangs roving the streets, with their guns and their attitude? A pack of predators you'll won't see in any purer form in the city. They probably even have an alpha who orders them around, who no one messes with., because he is the that guy, that badass motherfucker you don't want to mess with. Course, they are opposed by those guard dogs the police, those loyal hounds ready to bark and to bite to protect their territory: their jurisdiction. Course the gang also considers their streets their territory, and they fight over it. Thats just the way the city is. Ah, but the real alpha dogs are not on the streets but are in the big offices, they are the CEO's, the big men in big suits who don't tolerate people challenging their position. They got the most money, they got the power, they're not afraid to throw it around and let people now just how important they are. And thing is, the people at the top, they won't stop gathering money. They have an instinct to hoard it, to gather more and more even though they have more than enough, more money than most people ever see in their lifetime, also fearing something bad could happen.<br /> <br /> Thing is though, the entire economy is monetary barbarism. Its all about who is stronger, the strong companies survive and become successful, and the weak ones go out of business and die. Same with employees: you either work as best you can to survive you get fired and die. Employees either get promoted and thrive or get fired and die. Its all a competition, and you either win or you fail. Thing is, you got to put on appearances, you got to blend like a chameleon to peoples desires, you stick out your gonna get eaten up, company or employee. A company after all, has to change its colors with the times after all, convince people that they still get them, that they're still friendly when underneath they were always that money-making beast it always was. Similarly, the employees must change their colors to survive in their environment, to keep from being fired so that the company can save money, to keep themselves from becoming prey to feed the beast. <br /> <br /> Gets worse when your a politician: you got to unfold your feathers like a peacock, got to make everyone see how pretty you look around election time and make everyone choose the prettiest personality, parade yourself in front of everyone like a lion to show you mean business, and none of the other candidates can win after all: its either them or you and you've got to make sure your the one making the decisions, so that you can bark at the sheep to make them go where you want. Thats what you got to do, to be the alpha of everyone's pack, y'know? But your thinking: surely it can't be everywhere? what about school? but it is. Those popular kids are your alpha dogs, and everyone else is the herd. Cross them and you get ridiculed. However there is also the grades. You don't get good ones, you die. Good grades are how they determine who survives and who doesn't. Gotta parrot back all that info they're squeezing into you, or you won't get anywhere. Gotta imitate the good students or you won't have the info to earn your food. Course the teachers, they watching over you like cubs. They may care for you, but they also have to know when to throw you out the nest so that you have to spread your wings and fly on your own. This kind of thing is sink or swim eventually, and you gotta learn how to swim the social and mental currents to survive in this world.<br /> <br /> Even scientists and inventors got to deal with this: the one who can provide their evidence is the one who is the strongest position for their theory, and all the other theories die, the inventor who makes the best most usable tool gets the fame, not the guy who first came up with it. Thats urban nature for you. Its not about who came up with it first, its about who found enough muscle to put behind it to make sure everyone goes along with it. People think they're no longer beasts, but they're wrong. All they have done is change the rules of being a beast, what the prey is, and how to get it. The people here might use words and lies and such and so on instead of claw and fang, but they are still the apex predators because of it. My point is? Any one of these people could be a Lunar. Why, a Lunar might be all of these and more. Society is full of competition, and every competition is in some way the survival of the fittest. Personally, to think otherwise is kind of naive to my point of view. Our baser instincts are not so easily wiped out, they just show up in ways advantageous to us so we think nothing of it.<br /> <br /> Now if you'll excuse me, I've got to go find some prey to con out of their money...I am an apex predator of the urban jungle after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T14:03:00-07:00","id":700115,"title":"","content":"I am so excited for Lunars to better facilitate urban-origin characters, versus having to actively fight against both narrative and mechanics to pull it off effectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T14:59:20-07:00","id":700132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">having to actively fight against both narrative and mechanics to pull it off effectively</div> </div> </div> </div> How was this in Second Edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T15:58:31-07:00","id":700220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/700087-lunars-and-the-urban-jungle?p=700115#post700115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am so excited for Lunars to better facilitate urban-origin characters, versus having to actively fight against both narrative and mechanics to pull it off effectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>I often feel that too many people paid attention to the self-confessed propaganda from the Silver Pact in 1e, and not the passage in the second chapter that explicitly noted that Lunar selected whomever she damn well pleased as Chosen, disregarding even the &quot;hardscrabble life&quot; detail to provide examples like a really hot guy, or a general who warred with barbarians out of spite. But then, disproportionate word count, disproportionate attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}